// The peoples of the world.
//
// A culture is a name, a family, a colour and what most of it believes. The faith may be
// one entry or two: a people genuinely split down the middle is a fact about the Yoruba
// and the Albanians and the Lebanese, and flattening it to a majority would throw away the
// most interesting thing about them.
//
// Nothing here says where anybody lives. That is history/pops, because who lives where is
// a fact about 2024 and can be rewritten by a scenario without redefining the peoples.
//
// Later files win, so a mod that only wants to split one culture in two writes two lines.
//
// "country" is what a state this people founds is called, where it has a name of its own -
// Kurdistan, Catalonia. Without it a new state takes the name of the region it is founded on.
